<section
  id="faq"
  class="home-faq"
>
  <div class="site-container">

    <div class="home-faq__intro">

      <p class="home-faq__label">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </p>

      <h2>
        Common questions about sourcing with PACTSOL.
      </h2>

      <p>
        These answers explain the current PACTSOL sourcing model and help
        customers and suppliers understand how an enquiry may proceed.
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="home-faq__items">

      <details>
        <summary>
          What products can PACTSOL help source?
        </summary>

        <p>
          PACTSOL currently accepts enquiries across selected products within
          seven sourcing categories: packaging and dispatch consumables;
          maintenance and fabrication consumables; safety and PPE; material
          handling and warehouse MRO; general industrial replacement MRO;
          micro-irrigation and agricultural infrastructure; and low-risk solar
          O&M accessories. Product availability and sourcing support remain
          subject to requirement review and supplier confirmation.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          Is there a charge to submit a sourcing requirement?
        </summary>

        <p>
          No. Submitting a sourcing requirement for initial review is free.
          Where a buyer-paid sourcing or service fee applies, the applicable
          scope and fee will be communicated before the customer commits to
          the relevant service or transaction.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          Does PACTSOL guarantee product availability or supplier acceptance?
        </summary>

        <p>
          No. Product availability, supplier participation, specifications,
          quantities, pricing, delivery, and other commercial terms remain
          subject to sourcing, supplier confirmation, and the applicable
          transaction terms.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          Does PACTSOL select the supplier for the customer?
        </summary>

        <p>
          No. PACTSOL may help identify and coordinate suitable supply options
          and organize available commercial information. The customer remains
          responsible for supplier selection, commercial acceptance, and the
          final purchasing decision.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>
          Can manufacturers, distributors, and suppliers work with PACTSOL?
        </summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Relevant manufacturers, distributors, and suppliers may share
          their product capabilities with PACTSOL for consideration against
          suitable sourcing requirements. Sharing information does not
          guarantee an enquiry, order, appointment, or business opportunity.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
